Description: Copy the views of a stereo display at their own resolution
 .
 The image handed to the compositor held both views scaled to the size
 one view is shown at, so a top-and-bottom or side by side (half)
 display was stretched back to full size here and resized again by the
 compositor to the window.
 .
 Copy each view as the guest's frame carries it instead: a top-and-bottom
 1920x1080 frame becomes one 3840x540 image, a side by side (half) frame
 two 960x1080 views. The surface's viewport, which already has the size
 a view is shown at, gives the compositor the one resize.
 .
 The test checks the packed size and every sample of both views against
 the frame, for each HDMI 1.4b structure.
